doc.body:
Use with :obj:`LibTmux.Query <LibTmux.Query>`. All tokens belong to the tmux 3.3a baseline.
 The same physical window can occur at several indices in one session;
 :obj:`WindowLink <LibTmux.Snapshot#t:WindowLink>` retains each appearance. :obj:`active <LibTmux.Query.Link#v:active>` is contextual to the session.

doc.summary:
Rename the session targeted by a reference from this Server generation.
 The name is literal text. Earlier :obj:`Snapshot <LibTmux.Snapshot#t:Snapshot>` values keep their old names;
 call :obj:`capture <LibTmux.Server#v:capture>` for a new observation. Use :obj:`renameSessionWith <LibTmux.Server#v:renameSessionWith>` for a deadline.

doc.body:
Callback failures and cancellation keep their original exception class.
 Incomplete cleanup retains a :obj:`CleanupRecovery <LibTmux.Server#t:CleanupRecovery>` in the exception context;
 use :obj:`tryTmux <LibTmux.Server#v:tryTmux>` and :obj:`cleanupRecoveries <LibTmux.Server#v:cleanupRecoveries>` to keep that responsibility reachable.

doc.summary:
Adopt one endpoint within an existing Runtime and close only that handle
 after the callback. Other handles remain admitted under the shared limits;
 each adoption has its own :obj:`serverGeneration <LibTmux.Server#v:serverGeneration>`. Use :obj:`withServer <LibTmux.Server#v:withServer>` for one handle.
